# NOTE: git does not support trailing comments on a pattern line. A line like
#   *.har   # browser captures
# is treated as the literal pattern "*.har   # browser captures" and matches nothing.
# Every comment here therefore gets its own line. Verified by scripts/verify-ignores.sh.

# ── Credentials and personal data ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The tool never writes these into the project folder — they live in the OS config
# directory. These rules exist anyway, because someone debugging a problem will
# eventually put one here by hand, and that is the moment this file earns its keep.

# Browser network captures. Contain live session cookies.
*.har
har/
cookies.txt
cookies.json
session.json
config.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# ── Downloaded media ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never commit a child's photo. Not yours, not anybody's.
Brightwheel*Photos/
archive/
downloads/
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.heic
*.mp4
*.mov
*.png

# Documentation screenshots are the one exception: they come from the mock server
# and contain only synthetic, invented children.
!docs/images/
!docs/images/*.png

# ── Browser automation state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
user-data-dir/
playwright-state.json
storageState.json
.playwright/

# ── Build and tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Claude Code worktrees used by parallel agents
.claude/worktrees/
